      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is highly likely the fault of the World itself. Try going to a different World instead.\n\nThe Near Clip set in the World's Reference Camera is probably set to `0.3` instead of `0.01`. If the Reference Camera in that World was already set to `0.01`, this issue wouldn't happen.\n\n**At any time you are in a World where this issue happens, you can temporarily fix this yourself** by going to `VRChat Menu -> Settings -> Graphics -> Common -> Forced Camera Near Distance` and changing it to `Dynamic` or `Forced`.\n\nFor the majority of the most well-built Worlds out there, you won't have to do this often. But it's there if you need it.\n\n*Keep in mind, this setting will be reset when you restart VRChat because some Worlds can break if using `Forced` Near Distance.*",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
