      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hi, it's hard to be certain just from the image but I suspect that this might be due to the nose ramping upwards into your view camera and clipping through it.\n\nYou could try adjusting the position of the avatar's viewpoint within the head. Alternatively, you could also try fixing this by adding a new bone inside the head of your avatar that's weight painted to the top of the head so it \"flattens\" the head down to the snout as it gets shrunk away, and then including that bone in your custom head chop. This could stop the nose ramping upwards into your view.\n\nI'd be happy to help verify if this is an issue specific to this avatar if you want to share its ID (there's no need to make the avatar public if it's private).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
