      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61e26f1487ed3c342968ace2|full_name}: Thanks very much - in this case, I can see that the avatar's view point is at a position where it sees the inside of the nose beyond the point where it starts ramping upwards. You might be able to see this in your avatar project if you create a camera at the same position as your avatar's view point and look through it in the game view.\n\nThe above suggestions should help, or for your case you could also try just flattening the ridge on the nose with a new custom head chop bone so the camera switches to seeing the outside of the nose instead.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
